  ($qb$S11C01Q08$qb$, $qb$S11$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Senior leaders hold each other accountable:$qb$, $qb$Openly and professionally — mutual accountability is a feature of how the team operates$qb$, $qb$Moderately — some accountability exists but is not consistently practised$qb$, $qb$Weakly — leadership accountability is primarily downward, not horizontal$qb$, $qb$Not at all — senior leaders do not hold each other to account$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S11C01Q09$qb$, $qb$S11$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Diversity of perspective in the senior leadership team:$qb$, $qb$Is actively valued and reflected in how decisions are made$qb$, $qb$Is present — the team has diverse backgrounds but not always diverse thinking$qb$, $qb$Is limited — the leadership team is largely homogeneous in background$qb$, $qb$Is very limited — the team has little diversity and this is a known strategic blind spot$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
