  ($qb$S12C10Q06$qb$, $qb$S12$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The pace of digital transformation relative to competitors is:$qb$, $qb$Ahead — the organisation is transforming faster than most competitors$qb$, $qb$At pace — broadly keeping up with the competitive transformation rate$qb$, $qb$Behind — the organisation is transforming more slowly than most competitors$qb$, $qb$Significantly behind — digital transformation lag is a serious competitive risk$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S12C10Q07$qb$, $qb$S12$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The organisation's approach to scaling successful digital pilots is:$qb$, $qb$Structured and fast — successful pilots are scaled within months with defined investment and ownership$qb$, $qb$Generally effective — successful pilots are scaled but the process takes longer than it should$qb$, $qb$Inconsistent — some pilots are scaled; others remain pilots indefinitely$qb$, $qb$Poor — the organisation has many pilots but struggles to scale any of them$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S12C10Q08$qb$, $qb$S12$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Digital transformation investment is funded:$qb$, $qb$Strategically and sustainably — digital investment is a defined budget line with multi-year commitment$qb$, $qb$Adequately — investment is allocated annually with reasonable continuity$qb$, $qb$Inconsistently — digital investment competes with other priorities and is frequently cut$qb$, $qb$Poorly — digital transformation is underfunded and subject to frequent budget cuts$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S12C10Q09$qb$, $qb$S12$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Culture alignment with the digital transformation agenda is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — the organisational culture actively supports and accelerates digital change$qb$, $qb$Generally supportive — the culture does not actively resist digital transformation$qb$, $qb$Mixed — cultural pockets actively resist digital change and this is slowing progress$qb$, $qb$Misaligned — the organisational culture is a primary barrier to digital transformation$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S12C10Q10$qb$, $qb$S12$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Overall, the digital transformation maturity and roadmap:$qb$, $qb$Positions the organisation as a digital leader — transformation is a genuine competitive advantage$qb$, $qb$Shows meaningful progress — the organisation is on a credible transformation journey$qb$, $qb$Indicates early stage — significant transformation work remains ahead$qb$, $qb$Indicates a digital laggard — transformation pace is creating serious competitive risk$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true)
