  ($qb$S13C10Q02$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Financial wellbeing programmes or support in your organisation (salary advances, financial counselling, savings schemes) are:$qb$, $qb$Comprehensive — a range of meaningful financial support is available and actively promoted$qb$, $qb$Present — some financial wellbeing support exists$qb$, $qb$Minimal — only basic financial support is available$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — the organisation provides no financial wellbeing support beyond basic pay$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q03$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The organisation's pay frequency and structure supports employee financial wellbeing:$qb$, $qb$Well — pay frequency, structure, and advance options are designed with employee financial wellbeing in mind$qb$, $qb$Adequately — standard pay practices are in place$qb$, $qb$Partially — some aspects of pay practice create unnecessary financial stress for some employees$qb$, $qb$Poorly — pay timing or structure creates significant financial hardship for some employees$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q04$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Financial education and literacy support for employees in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Provided — the organisation offers financial education resources and workshops$qb$, $qb$Partially provided — some financial information is available$qb$, $qb$Minimal — limited financial information is available to employees$qb$, $qb$Not provided — the organisation does not offer financial education or literacy support$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q05$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Emergency financial support (hardship loans, advance payments) for employees in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Available and accessible — clear, rapid financial support is available for genuine hardship$qb$, $qb$Available but not widely known$qb$, $qb$Limited — emergency financial support is available only in exceptional circumstances$qb$, $qb$Not available — employees have no access to emergency financial support from the organisation$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q06$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The organisation's approach to pay transparency helps employees manage their financial lives:$qb$, $qb$Yes — clear pay communication helps employees plan and manage their finances$qb$, $qb$Partially — some pay transparency supports financial planning$qb$, $qb$Limitedly — limited pay transparency makes it difficult for employees to plan financially$qb$, $qb$No — lack of pay transparency creates unnecessary financial uncertainty for employees$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q07$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Retirement savings support and guidance in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Comprehensive — employer contributions, investment guidance, and retirement planning support are all provided$qb$, $qb$Adequate — a pension scheme and basic information are provided$qb$, $qb$Basic — a pension scheme exists but no guidance or planning support is offered$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — the organisation provides no retirement savings support$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q08$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Employee access to financial counselling or advice through the organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Available — financial counselling is offered as part of the EAP or benefits package$qb$, $qb$Available for some — access depends on the EAP and is not actively promoted$qb$, $qb$Not easily available — financial counselling is theoretically available but access is difficult$qb$, $qb$Not available — the organisation does not provide access to financial counselling$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q09$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The correlation between financial stress and absence, productivity, and engagement is tracked in your organisation:$qb$, $qb$Yes — the organisation tracks financial stress indicators and links them to wellbeing outcomes$qb$, $qb$Partially — some monitoring of financial wellbeing impact occurs$qb$, $qb$Not systematically — the connection is acknowledged but not tracked$qb$, $qb$Not at all — the organisation does not connect financial wellbeing to business outcomes$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S13C10Q10$qb$, $qb$S13$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Overall, employee financial wellbeing in your organisation:$qb$, $qb$Is actively managed and is a genuine component of the employee experience$qb$, $qb$Is acknowledged and some support is provided$qb$, $qb$Is recognised but inadequately supported$qb$, $qb$Is not considered — the organisation does not address employee financial wellbeing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true)
