  ($qb$S14C01Q01$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The tone from the top on compliance in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Unambiguous — leadership treats compliance as non-negotiable and models ethical behaviour$qb$, $qb$Generally strong — leadership supports compliance without always actively championing it$qb$, $qb$Mixed — compliance is valued in principle but leadership behaviour is sometimes inconsistent$qb$, $qb$Weak — leadership does not model compliance and this filters down$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q02$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$A compliance function or designated compliance responsibility:$qb$, $qb$Exists with adequate resource, authority, and independence$qb$, $qb$Exists but is under-resourced or lacks sufficient authority$qb$, $qb$Is informally assigned without dedicated resource$qb$, $qb$Does not exist — compliance is managed ad hoc without a defined owner$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q03$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Employee awareness of compliance obligations in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$High — all employees understand the compliance requirements relevant to their role$qb$, $qb$Adequate — most employees know their key obligations$qb$, $qb$Inconsistent — awareness varies significantly by role, level, and department$qb$, $qb$Low — most employees have limited awareness of their specific compliance obligations$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q04$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Compliance training in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Mandatory, role-specific, and regularly refreshed with completion tracked$qb$, $qb$Provided for most roles but not always role-specific or regularly updated$qb$, $qb$Available but not consistently completed or enforced$qb$, $qb$Non-existent or token — compliance training is not meaningfully provided$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q05$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Reporting of potential compliance breaches in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Encouraged and protected — employees feel safe reporting concerns without fear of retaliation$qb$, $qb$Generally safe — most employees would report a concern$qb$, $qb$Uncertain — employees are unsure whether reporting is safe$qb$, $qb$Not safe — fear of retaliation prevents employees from reporting compliance concerns$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q06$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The organisation's response when a compliance breach is identified is:$qb$, $qb$Fast, transparent, and proportionate — investigation and remediation happen promptly$qb$, $qb$Generally appropriate — breaches are investigated and addressed$qb$, $qb$Slow — investigations and remediation take longer than they should$qb$, $qb$Poor — compliance breaches are not consistently investigated or remediated$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q07$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Integration of compliance into business processes and systems in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Deep — compliance is built into workflows so the default action is the compliant action$qb$, $qb$Adequate — most key compliance requirements are built into processes$qb$, $qb$Partial — some compliance is process-embedded; other areas rely on individual knowledge$qb$, $qb$Weak — compliance relies primarily on individual awareness rather than process embedding$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q08$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The compliance risk register in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Current, comprehensive, and used in management decision-making$qb$, $qb$Maintained and reviewed periodically$qb$, $qb$Exists but is outdated or incomplete$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — the organisation does not maintain a compliance risk register$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S14C01Q09$qb$, $qb$S14$qb$, $qb$C01$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$Escalation of compliance issues in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Fast and structured — employees know exactly how to escalate and issues reach the right level quickly$qb$, $qb$Generally effective — escalation works but could be more structured$qb$, $qb$Slow — compliance issues often take too long to reach the right level$qb$, $qb$Poorly managed — compliance issues are not consistently escalated or resolved$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
